#
# Competency question: "For each grounded topological property, what is its
# defining law or boundary record?" This surfaces the machine-audited backing
# edge math:definingLaw: every declared topological property concept
# (math:ContinuousMap, math:ConnectedSpace, math:CompactSpace, and the T0-T4
# separation-axiom individuals) reports the logic:Formula defining law that
# grounds it — or, for compactness, the recorded logic:expressivenessBoundary
# boundary record math:compactnessBoundary. Read over the merged ontology (no
# fixture), the answer is exactly the eight property -> backing pairs. This is
# the query twin of the open, type-checked law-backing audit in structural.ttl.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>

SELECT ?property ?backing WHERE {
    ?property math:definingLaw ?backing .
}
ORDER BY ?property ?backing
